## Claim
Text: "The Iowa Farm Bureau, US says that it would no longer be endorsing US Republican Iowa Sen. Joni Ernst for her re-election"
Claim date: October 18, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Did the Iowa Farm Bureau issue an official statement on or before October 18, 2020, declaring that it would no longer endorse Joni Ernst for her re‑election to the U.S. Senate?
Answer: No, the search result does not contain any official statement from the Iowa Farm Bureau declaring that it would no longer endorse Joni Ernst for re‑election; instead, it reports that the Iowa Farm Bureau Political Action Committee designated Ernst as a "Friend of Agriculture" for the 2020 general election, indicating continued support.

Source URL: https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/FB-designates-Friends-of-Ag

### What is the exact wording or source of the Iowa Farm Bureau’s announcement regarding its endorsement of Joni Ernst?
Answer: The Iowa Farm Bureau’s announcement is an article on its website titled “FB designates Friends of Ag,” which states: “The Iowa Farm Bureau Political Action Committee (PAC), has designated Sen. Joni Ernst as a 'Friend of Agriculture' for the 2020 general election.” The source is [https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/FB-designates-Friends-of-Ag](https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/FB-designates-Friends-of-Ag).

Source URL: https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/FB-designates-Friends-of-Ag

### Did the Iowa Farm Bureau endorse any other candidate for the 2020 U.S. Senate election in Iowa, either Republican or Democrat?
Answer: Based on the search result, the Iowa Farm Bureau's political arm endorsed Republican Joni Ernst for the U.S. Senate election, but there is no mention of them endorsing any other candidate—Republican or Democrat—for that specific race.

Source URL: https://qctimes.com/news/state-and-regional/govt-and-politics/campaign-almanac-for-wednesday-september-9-2020/article_78f6dbc5-6272-547c-9de9-e2a78cefb8cf.html

### What was the timing of the Iowa Farm Bureau’s announcement relative to the 2020 general election (held on November 3, 2020)?
Answer: The search result does not mention the Iowa Farm Bureau ceasing its endorsement of Joni Ernst; instead, it reports that she was designated a "Friend of Agriculture" for the 2020 general election. The only timing reference provided is that the names were to be published in the September 9 or October 21 editions of the Iowa Farm Bureau Spokesman, which is well before the November 3, 2020 election, but the search result contains no information about any announcement regarding the withdrawal of endorsement prior to that date.

Source URL: https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/FB-designates-Friends-of-Ag

### Does the Iowa Farm Bureau have a formal endorsement process, and does it typically endorse candidates for federal office in Iowa?
Answer: Yes, the Iowa Farm Bureau has a formal endorsement process through its political arm, the IFBF PAC, which designates candidates as a “Friend of Agriculture” based on their support for issues impacting Iowa’s agricultural economy. The search result confirms that the Iowa Farm Bureau does typically endorse candidates for federal office in Iowa, as it endorsed both U.S. Senator Joni Ernst and former congressman David Young in the same election cycle.

Source URL: https://www.iowafieldreport.com/campaigns/ernst-endorsed-by-the-iowa-farm-bureau/

## Final Judgement
The key insight from the fact-check is that the Iowa Farm Bureau’s political action committee designated Joni Ernst as a "Friend of Agriculture" for the 2020 general election, which is a formal endorsement. There is no evidence of any statement from the Iowa Farm Bureau indicating that it would no longer endorse her; instead, all retrieved sources confirm continued support. The claim directly contradicts this evidence.

`refuted`

